<p class="subtitle">Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) — Project Planning Document<br>
Prepared by: Kabera Muhire David &nbsp;|&nbsp; Date: 22 May 2026</p>

<div class="note">
  This document defines the full Software Development Life Cycle for the Tramed digital transformation project. It serves as the planning foundation before any code is written.
</div>

<h2>1. What is the SDLC?</h2>
<p>The Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) is the process every professional software project follows. It ensures we build the right thing, in the right order, without wasting time. Every phase must be completed before moving to the next.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Phase</th><th>Name</th><th>What happens</th><th>Status</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>1</td><td>Planning</td><td>Define the goal, scope, and timeline</td><td>Done</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td>Requirements</td><td>What exactly does the system need to do?</td><td>Done</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td>Design</td><td>Wireframes, architecture, data model</td><td>In Progress</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4</td><td>Development</td><td>Writing the actual code</td><td>Not Started</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5</td><td>Testing</td><td>Does it work correctly?</td><td>Not Started</td></tr>
    <tr><td>6</td><td>Deployment</td><td>Put it on a real server for users</td><td>Not Started</td></tr>
    <tr><td>7</td><td>Maintenance</td><td>Fix bugs, add features over time</td><td>Not Started</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

