<h2>3. Phase 2 — Requirements</h2>
<p>Requirements define exactly what the system must do. They are divided into Functional (what it does) and Non-Functional (how it performs).</p>

<h3>3.1 Functional Requirements</h3>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Requirement</th><th>Priority</th><th>Phase</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>1</td><td>Daily sales dashboard — revenue, margins, trends, alerts</td><td>Must Have</td><td>Phase 1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>2</td><td>Data pipeline — import and process Ishyiga CSV exports</td><td>Must Have</td><td>Phase 1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>3</td><td>Stock alerts — flag products low on stock</td><td>Must Have</td><td>Phase 1</td></tr>
    <tr><td>4</td><td>Demand forecasting — predict what to reorder and when</td><td>Should Have</td><td>Phase 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>5</td><td>Stock anomaly detection — flag unusual discrepancies</td><td>Should Have</td><td>Phase 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>6</td><td>Supplier auto-reorder messages</td><td>Should Have</td><td>Phase 2</td></tr>
    <tr><td>7</td><td>Chronic medication reminders via WhatsApp</td><td>Could Have</td><td>Phase 3</td></tr>
    <tr><td>8</td><td>Customer loyalty tracker</td><td>Could Have</td><td>Phase 3</td></tr>
    <tr><td>9</td><td>AI sales trend analysis — seasonal and event patterns</td><td>Future</td><td>Phase 4</td></tr>
    <tr><td>10</td><td>Customer segmentation by purchase behaviour</td><td>Future</td><td>Phase 4</td></tr>
    <tr><td>11</td><td>Profit margin optimization recommendations</td><td>Future</td><td>Phase 4</td></tr>
    <tr><td>12</td><td>Predictive restocking — forecast quantities per supplier</td><td>Future</td><td>Phase 4</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>3.2 Non-Functional Requirements</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Works in any browser — no installation required for pharmacy staff</li>
  <li>Builds on top of Ishyiga — does not replace it</li>
  <li>Must be replicable for other pharmacies with minimal changes</li>
  <li>Data must be secure — staff login required</li>
  <li>Must work on the devices already available at the pharmacy</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Phase 3 — Design</h2>
<p>The design phase defines what we build before writing any code. It includes the tech stack, page map, and data model.</p>

<h3>4.1 Confirmed Technology Stack</h3>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Technology</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Frontend</td><td>HTML + CSS + Bootstrap + JavaScript</td><td>What staff see and click</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Backend</td><td>Node.js + Express.js</td><td>The brain — handles all logic and requests</td></tr>
    <tr><td>ORM</td><td>Prisma</td><td>Translates JavaScript into database queries</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Database</td><td>PostgreSQL</td><td>Stores all data permanently</td></tr>
    <tr><td>AI Integration</td><td>Claude API (Anthropic)</td><td>Reports, alerts, smart search</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Version Control</td><td>Git + GitHub</td><td>Tracks every code change</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>4.2 Application Architecture</h3>
<p>The application follows a three-tier architecture. The frontend never talks directly to the database — everything goes through the backend.</p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Pharmacy Equivalent</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>PostgreSQL</td><td>The Stock Room</td><td>All data lives here permanently</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Node.js + Express + Prisma</td><td>The Pharmacist</td><td>Fetches data, applies logic, returns results</td></tr>
    <tr><td>HTML / CSS / JavaScript</td><td>The Counter</td><td>What staff see — dashboards, forms, buttons</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>4.3 Pages to Build (MVP)</h3>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Page</th><th>URL</th><th>What it shows</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Dashboard</td><td>/dashboard</td><td>Daily KPIs, charts, stock alerts, transaction log</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sales</td><td>/sales</td><td>Full sales history, search and filter by date</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Stock</td><td>/stock</td><td>Current stock levels, low stock alerts, reorder list</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Upload</td><td>/upload</td><td>Upload new Ishyiga CSV export to update data</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Login</td><td>/login</td><td>Staff authentication — username and password</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>4.4 Data Model (What gets stored in the database)</h3>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Table</th><th>What it stores</th><th>Key fields</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>sales</td><td>Every sales transaction from Ishyiga</td><td>invoice_id, product_name, quantity, price, total, date, payment_method</td></tr>
    <tr><td>products</td><td>Product catalogue</td><td>product_code, product_name, category, supplier</td></tr>
    <tr><td>stock</td><td>Current stock levels per product</td><td>product_id, quantity, reorder_level, last_updated</td></tr>
    <tr><td>users</td><td>Staff login accounts</td><td>name, email, password_hash, role</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>5. Internship Phases</h2>
<div class="phase-box">
  <strong>Phase 1 — Audit &amp; Discovery:</strong> Technical discovery audit of Ishyiga usage, operations, stock, and customer flows. Produce written diagnosis report and priority list.
</div>
<div class="phase-box">
  <strong>Phase 2 — Implementation:</strong> Build no-code solutions independently. Develop software and AI components under technical supervision. Show progress every 2 weeks via video demo.
</div>
<div class="phase-box">
  <strong>Phase 3 — Results &amp; Packaging:</strong> Measure what improved. Write final case study. Package solution as replicable product for other pharmacies. Receive formal internship documentation.
</div>

<h2>6. What We Build First (MVP)</h2>
<p>The Minimum Viable Product (MVP) is the smallest version of the app that delivers real value. Based on the requirements, the MVP covers Requirements 1, 2, and 3:</p>
<ul>
  <li>A working web server (Node.js + Express)</li>
  <li>A database that stores Ishyiga sales data (PostgreSQL + Prisma)</li>
  <li>A dashboard that reads from the database and displays KPIs, charts, and stock alerts</li>
  <li>A CSV upload page so new Ishyiga exports can be loaded</li>
  <li>Staff login so only authorized users can access the system</li>
</ul>

